course: dictionary
lesson: 12326
title: Counselling: help that listens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Counselling is a noun, and its main meaning is help from a trained person who listens when you have problems or worries. «After her parents separated, Maya had counselling at school.» The clue is in the rest of the sentence: parents separating is a hard time, so counselling must be support for someone who is struggling.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The school counsellor listened and helped Sam think through his worries.» Listened, helped and worries all point to support for feelings, so counselling means help that listens. Notice that the person who gives counselling is a counsellor.
explain: Counselling can also mean advice in general, but this is a more formal use. «The lawyer gave the family some counselling about their choices.» Swap in the word advice and the sentence still makes sense, so advice is the right meaning here.
fact: Counselling is a noun. The verb is counsel, as in «to counsel a friend».
fact: «Counselling» means help and advice from a trained person who listens to someone with problems or worries.
fact: Many schools have a counsellor, someone children can talk to when life feels hard.
fact: Children may get counselling after a hard time, such as a family break-up, bullying, or the death of someone close.
fact: In American English the spelling is counseling, with one l. The British spelling is counselling, with two l's.
exercise: «After the big move, Ruby had counselling to help her feel better.» What is counselling here? | A type of school lunch | Lessons in drawing and painting | Running races in the park | *Help from a trained person who listens to worries
exercise: Which person is most likely to give counselling? | A gardener who plants trees | A baker who sells bread | *A counsellor trained to listen to children's worries | A bus driver who takes children to school
exercise: «The school counsellor helped Sam talk about his worries.» Find and copy the word that names the person who helps. | *counsellor | worries | Sam | talked
test: «Grief counselling» is help for people who are very sad after someone has died. What does grief counselling mean? | Learning to cook with others | *Help for people who are very sad after someone has died | A test at school | Listening to loud music
test: Which word is the verb, the word for giving counsel? | *counsel | counsellor | counselling | counsellors
exam: Jayden reads: «After the accident, the family went to counselling together.» Which meaning fits best? | The sound of a bell | *Help from a trained person who listens to worries | Wet, grey weather | A new kind of football game
